WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Dave: Good morning, Hank and John.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.240
I'm Dave. I’m the operations manager at DFTBA.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.540
This is the rest of our staff.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.520
This is Caenaan, the warehouse manager.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.309
Caenaan is the reason we now have a forklift
in the warehouse.

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.909
What’s the name of the forklift?

00:00:10.909 --> 00:00:13.139
Caenaan: Well, of course, it’s Forky McForkface.

00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:14.150
Dave: This is Rachel.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.020
She’s our head of creator support.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.060
She gets to deal with all our wonderful creators
on a daily basis.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.669
She’s helped design many of our products.

00:00:20.669 --> 00:00:22.659
And this is Meg, our head of customer service.

00:00:22.659 --> 00:00:25.669
Any time you get an email, it’s probably
coming from Meg.

00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:31.189
So the real reason we’re here today is to
introduce you to the person who created Pizzamas.

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:33.280
This is Valerie Barr.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.290
Say hello.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:35.190
Valerie: Hello.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.280
Dave: Valerie actually lives here in Missoula.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:42.270
She works for VidCon, but her claim to fame
in life, and really this is her lasting legacy,

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.220
is she designed Pizza John.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.140
Valerie: You’re welcome.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:50.640
Dave: So there is a long and storied back
history to the creation of Pizza John, which

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.970
led to Pizzamas.

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:56.860
Hank actually did a video last year where
he explained the backstory, right?

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:57.600
Valerie: Yes.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.940
Dave: And that link is down below, but give
us the ten-second version of Pizza John.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.700
Valerie: Well, John likes pizza.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.780
One time in a video, John had a mustache.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.960
Thus, all of this.

00:01:06.969 --> 00:01:08.849
Dave: And here we are, six years later.

00:01:08.849 --> 00:01:12.740
We created kind of our own Pizzamas museum
here, and we’re gonna have Valerie take

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:16.479
us on a tour through the illustrious history
of Pizzamas.

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:17.339
You ready to start?

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:17.860
Valerie: Yup.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:18.360
Dave: Let’s do it.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:18.860
Valerie: ‘Kay.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:23.020
2010. Pizza John. The Original. Well loved. Well worn. Classic.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:23.820
Meg: 2012

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:24.620
Dave: Green Pizza John

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:25.580
Valerie: Neon nineties Pizza John

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:28.780
Caenaan: Eyes eyes eyes eyes eyes eyes Pizza
John

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:29.780
Rachel: Vampire Pizza John

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:30.820
Meg: Evil Pizza John

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.160
Caenaan: 2013.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.280
Just the hoodie.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.100
Valerie: 2014

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.200
Rachel: Bowie Pizza John

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.200
Meg: Glowy Pizza John

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.200
Caenaan: Halftone Pizza John

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.360
Valerie: Obey Pizza John

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.360
Rachel: 2015

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.420
Caenaan: Warhol John

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:42.400
Meg: Rainbow Pizza John, our first charity
shirt

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.500
Valerie: Blue neon Pizza John

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.700
Caenaan: Pisa John

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.380
Rachel: Misfits Pizza John

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:49.240
Dave: Faux knitted Pizza John sweatshirt

00:01:49.249 --> 00:01:50.460
Rachel: Nebula John

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.420
Valerie: This year, as Hank talked about on
Monday, we asked our favorite designers to

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.319
design shirts, and Rachel is going to tell
you about that.

00:01:56.319 --> 00:02:01.139
Rachel: So this year we had a few different
artists.This one was designed by Judy Kaufmann.

00:02:01.139 --> 00:02:03.450
This one was designed by Sara Cervantes.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.700
The one right above me was Julia Pott.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.259
We have this one right here, which I did.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.930
We have Big John Pizzeria, designed by TEKST.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:13.250
We have Ming Doyle, which designed this pretty
sweet indigo one right here.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.880
And then we have the design duo Rude that
designed this one right here.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.530
Dave: Rachel, I hear there’s a few more
items in the 2016 Pizzamas collection.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.420
Rachel: Why yes there are, Dave.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.690
Dave: Are those pajama pants you’re wearing?

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:26.690
Rachel: They are.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.740
They are called the PJ-PJ.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:29.960
Dave: And are they soft?

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:31.910
Rachel: They’re very soft.

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:37.530
As Hank also talked about Monday, we will
have the personal pizza Pizzamas box, which

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:41.340
will contain quite a lot of things that you
can only get in the box.

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:46.750
It’ll have this hot and fresh shirt, a hot
and fresh notepad, a Pizza John pizza cutter

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:52.130
with a bottle opener, an apron with gold imprints,
and of course, the box.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:56.470
So just like last year, we wanted to have
an item that donated its proceeds to charity.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.460
This year we have the Pizza John pet leash.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:04.330
If you purchase this pet leash, 100% of its
profits will be going to the Animal Legal Defense Fund.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.610
If you have any questions about the Fund,
definitely go to the link down below.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.620
Wait a minute, what’s that?

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:21.680
Dave: This is a DFTBA sock that is only available
for purchase through the DFTBA Awesome Sox Club.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.860
This is the November sock, designed by Rachel.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:26.400
And Rachel, how many are left?

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.520
Caenaan: 500

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:33.190
Dave: That’s right, 500 more subscriptions
are left, so buy them soon. They're awesome.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:38.100
So thanks for joining us on this tour of the
Pizzamas museum here at the DFTBA warehouse.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.140
We’ll let the professionals take it from
here.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.940
Caenaan: Forky McForkface wants to remind
you: Don’t forget to be awesome.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:46.420
And John, we’ll see you tomorrow.

